        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(qa-lab): prevent Slack desktop bootstrap hangs",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where QA Lab Slack desktop smoke runs could wait indefinitely while fetching the NodeSource setup script, Node.js checksum or archive, or the pnpm archive.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe generated remote script now gives all four downloads a 10-second connection deadline and a 120-second total deadline. The verified Node.js and pnpm artifact downloads preserve their existing three finite retries, while the piped NodeSource script intentionally is not retried because replaying a partially emitted script into `bash` is unsafe. The existing Slack `auth.test` request remains bounded by its 15-second `AbortSignal.timeout` deadline.\n\n## User Impact\n\nQA operators now get a finite, logged bootstrap failure instead of a Slack desktop smoke run remaining stuck in a download.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Exact head: `a1c1de28ce6de0ba66aff6f8250a8a28adcf80ff`, rebased without patch changes onto `3e4b3b370f944f3e22c5104cd7d78c955fef8b2d`; the touched files are unchanged through current `main` at `b6989cbaf26ec35154d259f0e861d064477f3826`.\n- Generated-script assertions lock all four curl targets and deadlines, the three existing archive retry policies, and the existing `AbortSignal.timeout(15_000)` call.\n- Secretless live NodeSource probe returned HTTP 200 in 0.70s. [NodeSource distributions](https://github.com/nodesource/distributions)\n- Secretless live Node.js `v24.15.0` checksum probe returned HTTP 200 in 0.74s. [Node.js release files](https://nodejs.org/download/release/v24.15.0/)\n- Secretless live pnpm `11.2.2` tarball probe returned HTTP 200 in 1.20s. [pnpm package](https://www.npmjs.com/package/pnpm)\n- Secretless Slack `auth.test` probe without a token returned HTTP 200 with `not_authed`; no credential was used or printed. [Slack auth.test](https://api.slack.com/methods/auth.test)\n- Controlled no-response curl calibration with `--max-time 1` exited 28 after 1,012 ms.\n- `oxfmt --check` passed for both touched files; `git diff --check upstream/main...HEAD` passed.\n- Fresh Claude Sonnet autoreview: patch correct, confidence 0.95, no accepted/actionable findings.\n- Secretless fork [CI run 29400924097](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29400924097) passed: 50 jobs succeeded and 12 out-of-scope jobs skipped.\n- [CodeQL run 29400923917](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29400923917) passed all 7 security jobs; [Critical Quality run 29400923980](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29400923980) passed its 2 selected jobs and skipped 14 out-of-scope jobs.\n- AI-assisted: implemented with Codex and reviewed with Claude. I inspected and understand the generated-script behavior.\n\nThe curl deadline semantics follow the [official curl man page](https://curl.se/docs/manpage.html).\n",
        "branch": "alix/qa-slack-installer-timeouts",
